<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Albania</h1><p class="st-meta">1914 CE – 1925 CE · capital Durrës</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Albania's first internationally recognised state, a principality that survived foreign occupation in the First World War and was rebuilt as a nation in 1920.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conference-of-ambassadors">Conference of Ambassadors</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> made <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> an independent principality under the Great Powers' guarantee and chose the German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-prince-of-albania">Prince Wilhelm of Wied</a> as ruler. He arrived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a> on 7 March 1914, replacing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/provisional-government-of-albania">Provisional Government of Albania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essad-pasha-toptani">Essad Pasha</a>'s <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-central-albania">Republic of Central Albania</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Wied's rule collapsed within months amid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essad-pasha-toptani">Essad</a>'s intrigues, a Muslim peasant revolt in central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> and Greek-backed autonomy in the south; he left in September 1914. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> Italian, Austrian, Serbian, Greek and French troops occupied the country. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-lushnje">Congress of Lushnjë</a> in 1920 created a regency council, moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirana">Tirana</a> and secured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> membership.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The 1920s saw instability, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fan-noli">Fan Noli's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/june-revolution-albania">June Revolution</a> of 1924 overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">Ahmet Zogu</a> in December. In January 1925 a constituent assembly abolished the principality and created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albanian-republic">Albanian Republic</a>, with Zogu as president.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-albania.jpg" alt="Principality of Albania" width="320" height="460"><figcaption>Image: Achille Dardano · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1916_map_-_Carta_corografica_dell%27Albania_e_regioni_contermini_del_Montenegro,_Serbia_e_Grecia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1914 CE – 1925 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Durrës</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wilhelm of Wied, Fan Noli, Ahmet Zogu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Orthodox and Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Principality of Albania (1914-1925)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=principality-of-albania" aria-label="Principality of Albania on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5155 704 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Albania lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5475 960L5478 988M5475 960L5475 960M5475 960L5380 747M5475 960L5484 960M5475 960L5509 983M5475 960L5488 943M5475 960L5496 1000"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5478 988h0M5475 960h0M5380 747h0M5484 960h0M5509 983h0M5488 943h0M5496 1000h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5475 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5475 960h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Durrës. <a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=principality-of-albania">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
